Very interesting!  I'd make the various sources of vapor/poison gas
damage a couple of hit dice stronger in response to this.

If nonbreathing polymorph forms weren't already left unharmed by
amulets of strangulation, I'd think that would be a bug.

- John H.

L wrote:
> This patch does the following:
> * In their source mythos, towels are supposed to have a multitude of
> uses. However, towels only have two in-game uses - wiping and
> blindfolding. So, I implemented a third: you can now "wrap it round
> your head to ward off noxious fumes" as the data file puts it. Noxious
> fumes include stinking clouds, potion vapors, green/orange dragon
> breath, chest gas traps, and sleeping gas traps.
> * Amulets of strangulation also protect you from gaseous attacks.
> * Making strangulation useful: blessed amulets of strangulation can be
> worn without killing you.
> * Various breathless monsters (such as golems, zombies and such) are no
> longer harmed by strangulation.
